# WaterGuru dashboard - twice-daily fetch, publish, and alert.
#
# Install with:   crontab -e     (then paste, editing the path)
# Verify with:    crontab -l
#
# Two things bite people here, and both are handled below rather than in the
# environment: cron runs with a nearly empty PATH and no shell profile, and it
# mails you every line of output unless you redirect it. run_and_publish.sh
# fixes PATH itself and reads credentials from .env, so the crontab only has to
# say where the project lives and where the log goes.

SHELL=/bin/bash
MAILTO=""

# 8am and 8pm, local time of the machine's timezone.
# Don't go more often than this - WaterGuru's API does a full Cognito login on
# every run and isn't meant for polling.
0 8,20 * * *  WG_LOG=/home/YOU/waterguru-dashboard/data/cron.log /home/YOU/waterguru-dashboard/run_and_publish.sh

# Headless server with no Cloudflare deploy configured? Skip the deploy step:
# 0 8,20 * * *  WG_SKIP_DEPLOY=1 WG_LOG=/home/YOU/waterguru-dashboard/data/cron.log /home/YOU/waterguru-dashboard/run_and_publish.sh

# Ollama running on a different machine than this one (e.g. dashboard on a
# Linux box, models on the Mac Mini)? Point at it - and make sure that Mac is
# started with OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 so it listens beyond localhost:
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://mac-mini.local:11434
#
# Anything set here as a cron environment variable also works in .env, which is
# usually the tidier place for it.
